.TH SHB-INIT 1 "October 2026" "SecretHarbor 0.1.0" "SecretHarbor Manual"
.SH NAME
shb-init \- Initialize SecretHarbor host integration and project policy
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBshb init [path] [--yes] [--force]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Configures SecretHarbor host-level security for the current project. Automatically discovers supported AI agents (Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, Aider, Cline) and desktop environments (Cursor, VS Code), installs transparent launcher shims (~/.secretharbor/shims), configures shell profile PATH (~/.zshrc, ~/.bashrc), scans for running agent processes, and initializes secretharbor.yaml if not present. Shims persist across system reboots.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB-y\fR, \fB--yes\fR
Automatically restart unprotected running agents without interactive confirmation
.TP
\fB-f\fR, \fB--force\fR
Overwrite existing secretharbor.yaml with current default template
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
$ \fBshb init\fR
.TP
$ \fBshb init --yes\fR
.TP
$ \fBshb init --force\fR
.TP
$ \fBshb init ./my-project/secretharbor.yaml\fR
.SH SEE ALSO
shb(1)
.SH WEBSITE
https://github.com/logn10/SecretHarbor
